{
  "_readme": [
    "GST rate per HSN, used to catch a product priced at the wrong slab.",
    "",
    "source=catalogue-unanimous means the rate was taken from a shop's own records because",
    "every product it holds under that HSN agreed. It is evidence, not authority: if the rate",
    "was keyed wrong the first time and copied since, the agreement is unanimous and wrong.",
    "Such an entry only confirms what the shop already believes, so it never contradicts a",
    "catalogue that agrees with itself.",
    "",
    "source=verified means someone checked the entry against the GST schedule. Only a verified",
    "entry can overrule a shop, which is what catches a rate that is wrong everywhere.",
    "",
    "Promote an entry by checking the rate against the schedule and changing its source to",
    "verified. Do not promote one on the strength of it looking right -- the whole point of the",
    "distinction is that a shop's own consensus is exactly what cannot be trusted here."
  ],
